 75KR c  2012St19: {+40}Ca beam at E=180, 185 MeV provided by the XTU tandem    
 75KR2c  accelerator of the Laboratori Nazionali di Legnaro. Targets=1 and      
 75KR3c  0.9 mg/cm{+2} {+40}Ca. Gamma rays detected by the |g-spectrometer      
 75KR4c  EUROBALL. Charged particles detected by the Italian Silicon Sphere     
 75KR6c  (ISIS). Neutrons detected by the Neutron Wall (NWALL). Measured E|g,   
 75KR7c  I|g, (neutron)|g-, |g|g-coin, DCO. Deduced levels, J, |p, branching    
 75KR8c  ratios, bands, multipolarity, configurations. Comparison with          
 75KR9c  configuration-dependent cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky approach.           
 75KR cG $ DCO values correspond to gates on |DJ=2, quadrupole (E2) transition. 
 75KR2cG Expected DCO values are 1.00 {I3} for |DJ=2, quadrupole and 0.55 {I2}  
 75KR3cG |DJ=1, dipole transitions. However, the values listed in table I of    
 75KR4cG 2012St19 follow an opposite trend.                                     
 75KR cG $ 2012St19 give branching ratios also deduced from their relative      
 75KR2cG intensity data. These values are not listed here                       
 75KR cG RI(X)$ Branching ratio of 0.26 {I2} for 171.3|g and 0.74 {I6} for      
 75KR2cG 358.5|g listed in table I of 2012St19 are incorrect since intensity    
 75KR3cG of 179.0|g is not considered. See 1998Sk01 for correct branching ratios
